The first thing to say is that this is clearly a bug. What isn't quite
so clear is what's falling over first - the game or gtkhack. Assuming
it's repeatable, can I impose on you to look for the core file. It
should either be in the directory you ran gtkhack from (if it relates
to gtkhack) or (if it relates to the game) in the slashem playground
which with the RPMs is /var/games/slashem.

Having found the core file, you can confirm which program created it
as follows:

% file core
core: ELF 32-bit LSB core file of 'gtkhack' (signal 3), Intel 80386,
version 1, from 'gtkhack'
%

and then get a backtrace with one of the following (depending on whether
it was created by gtkhack or slashem):

% gdb /usr/lib/games/slashem/slashem core
[snip]
(gdb) bt
#0  <backtrace output here>
(gdb) quit
%

% gdb /usr/games/gtkhack core
[snip]
(gdb) bt
#0  <backtrace output here>
(gdb) quit
%

If you could possibly file a bug in our bugtracker:

http://sourceforge.net/bugs/?group_id=9746

detailing what happened (as above) and the backtrace produced by gdb,
that would be most helpful.

